hifiberry-tidal-connect (1.0.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian packaging of the Tidal Connect receiver as a HiFiBerry
    extension, installable from the HiFiBerry OS Web UI.
  * Ships the Docker build context, the four systemd units, and the players.d /
    audiocontrol / configserver drop-ins previously written by install.sh.
  * The container image is built on-device by a retryable oneshot unit
    (tidal-connect-build.service) rather than in the package maintainer script;
    the runtime tidal-connect.service is gated on a build stamp so a failed
    build never corrupts package state.
  * postinst generates the system-specific .env and docker-compose.yml and, on
    Pi 5 / CM5, switches to the 4K-page kernel and requests a reboot.

